SUPERSEDING PRIMARY-AUDIT CORRECTION:
The first fail-fast reproduction disproved the earlier guarded-build claim.
The compile-time type guard failed on the actual m68k shims: size_t and
uint32_t have different C types. A root command had chained a later hash
print/SSH task after that compiler failure, so a stale7fa executable was
mistakenly presented as a successful guarded rebuild. The failed compiler log
is retained. Reviewer conclusions conditional on that claimed build do not
establish compatible types. This is a microprobe qualification error, not a
core/production-handler change.

Root replaced direct/cast sparse function pointers with symmetric exact-size_t
adapters and explicit uint32 conversion, retained a32-bit-width assertion,
and advanced the micro protocol to2. The corrected actual build succeeds and
the fail-fast build-probe.sh reproduces SHA256
0b9a67a9554a1a4ef594f0bde18efbe6d2be5a63db662578eff61b58d41266a4.
Initial protocol1 runs and their consumers remain in micro/ and
micro-initial-parser/ as explicitly nonqualifying exploratory evidence.
Only freshly recorded protocol2 runs in micro-typed/ may support the final
micro timing/ABI conclusion. Production/probe handlers are unchanged; their
pilot, deep and normal inventories remain valid.

